{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03631",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.99,
      "end_seconds": 3.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Good afternoon, how are you today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 5.64,
      "end_seconds": 12.18,
      "duration_seconds": 6.54,
      "text": "Mm, hi doctor, I got here as fast as I could."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 13.67,
      "end_seconds": 19.64,
      "duration_seconds": 5.97,
      "text": "hello, doctor i'm here with them in case I can help"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.09,
      "end_seconds": 22.67,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "busy day out there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.88,
      "end_seconds": 28.07,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "Always is. The traffic coming in was terrible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.31,
      "end_seconds": 32.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "so what can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 34.15,
      "end_seconds": 39.87,
      "duration_seconds": 5.72,
      "text": "Erm, we came because of an itchy red rash on the chest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.89,
      "end_seconds": 45.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "when was the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.89,
      "end_seconds": 48.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "probably about a week. Yeah"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.65,
      "end_seconds": 54.78,
      "duration_seconds": 5.13,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.04,
      "end_seconds": 63.98,
      "duration_seconds": 7.94,
      "text": "right, a eight out of ten, I suppose it sort of comes and goes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.72,
      "end_seconds": 67.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.15,
      "end_seconds": 84.44,
      "duration_seconds": 15.29,
      "text": "it usually comes with a mild temperature. Actually, um, about mild temperature, it happens every other day. And spreading over a week as well, since yesterday"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.02,
      "end_seconds": 92.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.75,
      "text": "Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.19,
      "end_seconds": 110.01,
      "duration_seconds": 12.82,
      "text": "I work in accounts at a hospital. My husband and I live above the shop. Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.66,
      "end_seconds": 114.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.74,
      "end_seconds": 124.19,
      "duration_seconds": 7.45,
      "text": "It's allopurinol, 100 milligrams, once a day. It's fluoxetine, 20 milligrams, every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.41,
      "end_seconds": 128.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.27,
      "end_seconds": 134.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "My cousin has psoriasis. My daughter has type 1 diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.4,
      "end_seconds": 141.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.73,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.16,
      "end_seconds": 146.19,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "No, nothing as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 148.13,
      "end_seconds": 159.49,
      "duration_seconds": 11.36,
      "text": "actually, you know, I remember she had some kind of reaction to naproxen before i couldn't swear to it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.24,
      "end_seconds": 163.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Maybe, but I don't recall it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.92,
      "end_seconds": 166.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Okay, I'll note both of those."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.93,
      "end_seconds": 179.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.35,
      "end_seconds": 201.28,
      "duration_seconds": 20.93,
      "text": "Yes, gout. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite. Uh, uh, I've had depression, yes. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.82,
      "end_seconds": 204.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.33,
      "end_seconds": 209.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Nothing, I haven't had any operations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.66,
      "end_seconds": 223.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Did you get facial swelling, mouth sores or blistering?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 224.63,
      "end_seconds": 232.37,
      "duration_seconds": 7.74,
      "text": "So, you know, no facial swelling, mouth sores or blistering, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.09,
      "end_seconds": 234.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "How about breathing difficulty?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 236.23,
      "end_seconds": 238.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "Definitely no breathing difficulty."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.1,
      "end_seconds": 242.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "How are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 243.21,
      "end_seconds": 247.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Bowels are regular, um, nothing odd."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.07,
      "end_seconds": 252.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Anything with your heart, like skipped beats or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 253.4,
      "end_seconds": 256.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "no, uh, that's been fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 257.03,
      "end_seconds": 268.21,
      "duration_seconds": 11.18,
      "text": "okay, so the vitals from earlier pulse 69, temperature is 36.7 degrees, respiratory rate 17, oxygen saturation is 99 percent, pressure 125 over 82."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.62,
      "end_seconds": 271.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "good, thank you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.53,
      "end_seconds": 277.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.31,
      "end_seconds": 279.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "Breathe out slowly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.78,
      "end_seconds": 305.45,
      "duration_seconds": 7.67,
      "text": "There is a fine pink rash across the chest and arms, with no blistering and the mouth is clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.23,
      "end_seconds": 312.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.35,
      "end_seconds": 353.55,
      "duration_seconds": 23.2,
      "text": "So where does that leave us? I can't pin this down yet. We're looking at a drug rash probably from allopurinol or a viral rash. Please stop the allopurinol and don't restart it until we've spoken to the clinic. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 355.14,
      "end_seconds": 359.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "okay, uh, that makes sense thanks for explaining"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 360.42,
      "end_seconds": 361.8,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}